  "purpose": "One frozen purchase-independent internal preservation pilot. Real Apple identity verification and fixed participant/period/quota admission are preserved. Pending registrations do not create owners, sessions or access. Pilot eligibility is checked in reservation and commit; no billing account or active entitlement is fabricated. Release preparation enables only preservation with an internal-only signed export; all billing flags remain OFF and normal release defaults remain OFF. Server owner recovery/KMS dependencies and production gates are not implicitly enabled by source/config changes. Direct backend tests and independent review cover pilot/recovery/auth boundaries; native build, signing/privacy, Photos bootstrap, all runtime boundaries on both existing iOS versions, and two native operations (OFF entries hidden; pilot consent/save-result recovery) remain required. Actual device Apple sign-in, record upload, fresh-session restoration and ZIP remain separate live evidence. Widget rendering/selection source and targets are unchanged, so Widget galleries are omitted; no pass is inferred for omitted or failed jobs. This v3 native route is unmeasured and does not inherit earlier scope timing or UI proof.",
  "visualReview": "native-ui-required",
